    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners. When a create request includes an ISO `birthDate`, the owner now returns `ageBand` as `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), computed as full years between `birthDate` and the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges made, following the existing derived-field conventions:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` input schema, and a read-only `ageBand` string enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` output schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, column `birth_date`) with getter/setter, so the value survives the POST \u2192 GET round trip. MapStruct maps it by name on both `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` and `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto`.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `ageBand` to a new default `ageBand(Owner)` helper that uses `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and returns the enum, or `null` when no birth date is present (mirroring the existing `contactPreference` enum mapping).\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (hsqldb is the profile the tests use; the others kept in sync).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT` against today's registration date) passes, and a `null` birthDate correctly yields no `ageBand`, keeping existing behavior backward-compatible.",
